# Applied by live-build with debconf-set-selections BEFORE package installation.
#
# Two packages of the explicit firmware list (config/package-lists/
# cham3_firmware.list.chroot) ask for acceptance of their vendor licence in
# their preinst and refuse to install without it:
#   firmware-ipw2x00  Intel PRO/Wireless 2100/2200/2915 firmware
#   firmware-ivtv     Conexant/Hauppauge ivtv TV-capture firmware
# Under the earlier --firmware-chroot true design, live-build's chroot_firmware
# stage preseeded exactly these two answers itself. With the explicit list it no
# longer does, so they are stated here.
#
# Owner decision recorded 2026-10-12 (M1 repair cycle): accept both licences for
# the development image, keeping all 42 approved firmware packages; to be revisited
# before any public release (docs/tasks/M1-bootable-desktop-distribution.md).
firmware-ipw2x00 firmware-ipw2x00/license/accepted boolean true
firmware-ivtv firmware-ivtv/license/accepted boolean true
